        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="_title" value="&lt;b&gt;CRO vs HIG Pattern SPA_Internal_04 v1: Conformance and Declared Deviations&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontColor=#1F4E79;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="26" width="1640" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_subt" value="The Hartford EDS Claims  |  Draft for architecture review  |  v0.4 (pattern SPA_Internal_04)  |  2026-10-26" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#555555;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="58" width="1640" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_rule" value="" style="shape=line;html=1;strokeColor=#1F4E79;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="81" width="1640" height="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_x0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;ADOPTED AS WRITTEN&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Users: HIG employees on HIG-joined devices, on the&lt;br&gt;corporate network only&lt;br&gt;All traffic over Direct Connect; no internet path&lt;br&gt;Hosting in the LOB CloudOps account, us-east-1&lt;br&gt;VPC with private subnets across 2 AZs&lt;br&gt;Route 53 private hosted zone: app. and api. names&lt;br&gt;ACM certificates; TLS 1.2+ on 443 everywhere&lt;br&gt;Private REST API Gateway + execute-api VPC endpoint&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;+ custom domain + resource policy&lt;br&gt;API Gateway provisioned with the internal module&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;terraform-aws-apigateway-v1; no community modules&lt;br&gt;SPA authenticates with MSAL.js, OAuth 2.0 auth code&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;+ PKCE; no implicit flow, no client secret&lt;br&gt;Azure AD SSO backed by the device PRT; the SPA never&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;reads, stores or forwards the PRT&lt;br&gt;Lambda Authorizer, VPC-enabled, validates every&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;request: JWKS signature, issuer, audience, expiry,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;group / role claims; stateless&lt;br&gt;Authorizer returns a scoped IAM policy (Allow / Deny)&lt;br&gt;Lambda APIs invoked directly by API Gateway&lt;br&gt;Security groups: authorizer and Lambdas accept only&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the API Gateway path; no inbound from elsewhere&lt;br&gt;Tag-based IAM for administration of compute&lt;br&gt;CloudWatch logs and metrics, forwarded to Splunk per&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;the HIG CloudWatch-to-Splunk design&lt;br&gt;CloudTrail enabled for API activity audit&lt;br&gt;Retries with exponential backoff and jitter&lt;br&gt;Request metadata stored for idempotency (DynamoDB&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;in-flight lock and summary versions)&lt;br&gt;Consistent error codes to consumers (401/403/404/&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;409 in-progress / 202 queued)&lt;br&gt;HIG naming convention and mandatory tags&lt;br&gt;Route 53 failover for DR; repoint app CNAME&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="120" width="400" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_x1" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;ADAPTED: DEVIATION DECLARED WITH JUSTIFICATION&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;D1&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Static content served from S3 through the private API Gateway&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(HTTP proxy integration) instead of ECS Fargate + nginx + static ALB.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Why: the pattern itself (section 12, item 1) allows static delivery via&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;API Gateway. The CRO bundle is a few MB of HTML/JS/CSS with no server&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;logic. A container cluster across AZs adds patching, scaling, images&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;and cost while adding no control: the network boundary (VPC endpoint,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;private DNS, Direct Connect) is identical. Fewer components, smaller&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;attack surface. Reversible: the bundle can move to Fargate later&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;without changing the SPA or the API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;D2&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Fine-grained authorization performed inside the Lambda Authorizer&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;instead of a separate Authorize API.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Why: the pattern calls the Authorize API &quot;when needed&quot;. CRO's rule is&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;two DynamoDB reads (ENT# for the user, CLAIM# for the claim). A second&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;service adds a network hop, a failure point and a deployment with no&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;added control. The authorizer still returns the scoped IAM policy the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;pattern requires. Reversible: split into an Authorize API if the rule&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;set grows (hierarchies, exceptions) with no change to callers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;D3&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Static content unauthenticated at the edge.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Why: permitted by the pattern (section 5) when the bundle holds no HIG&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;confidential or proprietary content. The CRO bundle contains UI code&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;only; all claim data is fetched through the authorized API path.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;If a reviewer disagrees, the same gateway route can require the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;bearer token with no architecture change.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;D4&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DR scoped to the metal tier: Pilot Light (cold standby).&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Why: CRO is a handler convenience tool, not a claims-processing&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;dependency. Terraform redeploys the Lambdas, authorizer and gateway&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;to the secondary region; DynamoDB uses a global table; S3 snapshot&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;bucket uses cross-region replication; Route 53 failover repoints&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;app. and api. names. RTO/RPO to be confirmed against the tier.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;WHY THIS IS THE STRONGER POSITION&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each adaptation removes components rather than adding them. The security&lt;br&gt;controls the pattern exists to enforce (private network, enterprise SSO,&lt;br&gt;per-request token validation, scoped authorization, audit) are all&lt;br&gt;present. What is removed is infrastructure that serves heavyweight&lt;br&gt;ECS applications and would be idle in CRO.&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="460" y="120" width="560" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_x2" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;NOT APPLICABLE&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;VPC Link + internal API ALB&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Pattern: Lambda APIs are&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;invoked directly; CRO has&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;no ECS / EKS / EC2 backend&lt;br&gt;API ALB security group rules&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;No API ALB exists&lt;br&gt;ECS target-tracking scaling,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;task sizing, load tests&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Replaced by Lambda reserved&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;concurrency and SQS caps&lt;br&gt;Static ALB&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Removed with D1&lt;br&gt;On-premises ADFS&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Assumed Azure AD only&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(open item 2)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;OUTSIDE THE PATTERN&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everything behind the API:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;SQS, worker Lambda, DynamoDB,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;S3 snapshots, KMS CMKs&lt;br&gt;Snowflake ingest and writeback&lt;br&gt;GCP: Agent Engine, Gemini,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Cloud Trace, WIF&lt;br&gt;These follow the EDS Claims&lt;br&gt;GenAI NFR patterns (Hot Path)&lt;br&gt;and the earlier SIU review.&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1050" y="120" width="310" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_x3" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;OPEN ITEMS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Metal tier for CRO, and&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the numeric RTO / RPO&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; that follow from it&lt;br&gt;2&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Confirm Azure AD only&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; (no ADFS) as target&lt;br&gt;3&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Confirm internal module&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; supports private REST&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; API + S3 proxy route&lt;br&gt;4&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Splunk index / log&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; retention for audit&lt;br&gt;5&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Reviewer acceptance of&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; D1 and D3; fallback is&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Fargate + static ALB&lt;br&gt;6&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Role product columns&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; available in Snowflake&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; (LOB, office, adjuster,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; secured-claim access)&lt;br&gt;7&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Whether all CRO-Handlers&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; may read all flagged&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; claims (collapses L3)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1F4E79&quot;&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pilot: one LOB or office&lt;br&gt;Handlers already in Azure&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;AD; group created by IAM&lt;br&gt;Direct Connect and VPC&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;endpoints exist in the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;LOB account (landing zone)&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;fontFamily=Arial;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1390" y="120" width="280" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>